; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; §9.46 Int control probe
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; A small int-domain task-args curriculum used as a control alongside
; the §9.46 strings probe. The point of this file is NOT to measure how
; many tasks the M-chain can solve — it's to confirm that the M-chain
; integration path works at all on simple integer multi-arg tasks
; before we draw any conclusions from a string-domain failure.
;
; Each task is intentionally trivial. If even one of these fails, the
; problem is in the integration, not the strings probe.
;
; Concatenate with m_pool + m13 + m7..m12 + m_chain in front, then
; run via `selph grow-v2`. Expected outcome: 3/3 solves, all via
; either Flat (cheap enumeration) or custom:m-chain.

; M8 form 1 analogue — output is a non-trivial constant.
; 17 isn't in any input row, so Flat can only reach it via affine
; fit / data-atom seeding. Forces the M-chain to be the credited
; solver, not Flat-with-tiny-budget.
(task-args "const_17" 2
  ((1 1) 17) ((2 3) 17) ((5 7) 17) ((10 0) 17) ((0 0) 17))

; M10 affine analogue — output = a + 2*b. Affine fit over both atoms.
(task-args "a_plus_2b" 2
  ((1 1) 3) ((3 4) 11) ((5 6) 17) ((10 20) 50) ((0 0) 0))

; M11 product analogue — output = 3*(a*b). Product fit with scale.
(task-args "three_ab" 2
  ((1 2) 6) ((3 4) 36) ((5 6) 90) ((2 7) 42) ((0 9) 0))

; M9 unary wrap analogue — output = a*a (but no `square` in env).
; Forces M9 to wrap a base atom or M11 form 4 to fire on a self-product.
(task-args "a_squared" 2
  ((2 0) 4) ((3 0) 9) ((5 0) 25) ((7 0) 49) ((10 0) 100))

; M12 structural pair analogue — output = a + (b * b).
(task-args "a_plus_bsq" 2
  ((1 2) 5) ((3 3) 12) ((4 5) 29) ((0 6) 36) ((10 1) 11))
